## Design Rules

### Rule 1: Text Width
characters_per_line = (width - 20) / font_size. Keep ≤ 75%.

### Rule 2: Text Height
Count <p> tags, calculate lines, look up in table.

### Rule 3: Alignment
Vertical: inner.top = outer.top + (outer.height - inner.height) / 2
Horizontal: inner.left = outer.left + (outer.width - inner.width) / 2

### Rule 4: Symmetry
Use exact same values for parallel elements. Gap consistency.

### Rule 5: Text with Background Shape
Shape first (20px padding), then center text inside.

### Rule 6: Spacing
Title to body: 35-50px. Between paragraphs: 20-30px. Element to edge: ≥ 50px.

### Rule 7: Font Sizes
Main title: 32-36px. Subtitle: 24-28px. Key points: 18-20px. Body: 16-18px.

---

## Pre-Output Checklist

1. All text heights from lookup table
2. Text width calculation verified
3. Elements within 50px margins
4. No LaTeX in TextElement
5. LineElement width is stroke (2-6), not length

## Output Format

Output valid JSON only. No explanations, no code blocks.
